{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>You shall not go out.</b> Like the high priest, about whom it is said: ״כי נזר שמן משחת אלקיו עליו.״ And this is what we learned in Torat Kohanim: ״ויקרא משה אל מישאל ואל אלצפן״ — but not to Elazar and Itamar; from here that priests do not become impure through the dead, etc. And do we really need to learn this from here? Were not many passages spelled out in the Torah regarding the warning of priestly impurity? And furthermore, Elazar and Itamar were ordinary priests — why did they not become impure for their brothers, when we find that Moses said to Mishael and Elzaphan: ״קרבו שאו את אחיכם״? Rather, this is its meaning: from here the Sages said that priests on the day of their anointing do not become impure for any dead person, for even ordinary priests on the day of their anointing have the status of a high priest — for we find that these were warned on the day of their anointing in all the laws of the high priest."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:04.851394838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}